const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"Engle提出ARCH思想，允许时间序列的条件方差随过去信息而变化。 阅读时先把它理解为一个被界定的问题，而不是可以脱离样本、时间和制度环境的结论。",en:"“Autoregressive Conditional Heteroscedasticity with Estimates of the Variance of United Kingdom Inflation” frames a bounded research question. Read the stated question together with the named sample, dates, and institutional setting rather than treating it as a conclusion that automatically travels to another market or period."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2307/1912773",label:{zh:"Econometrica (1982) · 来源说明",en:"Econometrica (1982) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"模型把均值方程与条件方差方程分开指定，用过去误差等信息描述波动的时变性。 这说明比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系是研究合同的一部分；改变其中任何一项，都可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"For “Autoregressive Conditional Heteroscedasticity with Estimates of the Variance of United Kingdom Inflation”, the source describes a deliberate comparison, observation window, and control relation. Those choices are part of its research contract: changing one can change the proposition being tested, even when the method label remains the same."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2307/1912773",label:{zh:"Econometrica (1982) · 来源说明",en:"Econometrica (1982) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"需要保留原始时间序列、频率、缺口、均值设定、残差定义与用于估计的完整时间窗口。 数据字段、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原始研究分开记录，不能仅凭同名变量或最终修订数据就视为可比。",en:"For “Autoregressive Conditional Heteroscedasticity with Estimates of the Variance of United Kingdom Inflation”, keep the fields, their availability timing, and the sample filters separate from the original study. A same-named variable, later-revised database, or matching end-of-period date is not automatically a comparable input."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2307/1912773",label:{zh:"Econometrica (1982) · 来源说明",en:"Econometrica (1982) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"ARCH说明方差不必恒定；它不是对任何金融价格自动适用的波动预测承诺。 它支持的是该来源所描述的经验或理论关系；它本身不把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"For “Autoregressive Conditional Heteroscedasticity with Estimates of the Variance of United Kingdom Inflation”, the source supports only the empirical or theoretical relation it describes. It does not turn association, model fit, or historical performance into causality, a directly executable procedure, or a guarantee about subsequent outcomes."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2307/1912773",label:{zh:"Econometrica (1982) · 来源说明",en:"Econometrica (1982) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"检验残差结构、参数约束、估计样本和诊断结果，并区分条件方差估计与未来真实波动。 在做后续分析前，应把这些选择写入版本化的研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Before extending “Autoregressive Conditional Heteroscedasticity with Estimates of the Variance of United Kingdom Inflation”, record its sample, timing, construction choices, and source edition in a versioned note. Keep the primary-source link and access date so a later reader can distinguish a changed definition from a changed result."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2307/1912773",label:{zh:"Econometrica (1982) · 来源说明",en:"Econometrica (1982) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 Econometrica (1982)。模型遗漏、结构变化和极端尾部都可能使历史拟合无法代表之后的风险。 若需要量化结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites Econometrica (1982) for “Autoregressive Conditional Heteroscedasticity with Estimates of the Variance of United Kingdom Inflation”. Its public description defines the boundary. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2307/1912773",label:{zh:"Econometrica (1982) · 来源说明",en:"Econometrica (1982) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“Autoregressive Conditional Heteroscedasticity with Estimates of the Variance of United Kingdom Inflation”所公开说明的研究问题与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。模型遗漏、结构变化和极端尾部都可能使历史拟合无法代表之后的风险。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “Autoregressive Conditional Heteroscedasticity with Estimates of the Variance of United Kingdom Inflation”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
